### Replication of the Problem

```js
import { ListrEnquirerPromptAdapter } from '@listr2/prompt-adapter-enquirer'
import { Listr } from 'listr2'

const task = new Listr([{
    title: 'parent',
    task: async(ctx, task) => {
      const prompt = task.prompt(ListrEnquirerPromptAdapter)

      await prompt.run({
        type: 'confirm',
        message: 'a',
      });

      return task.newListr([
        {
          title: 'child1',
          task: async(ctx, task) => {
            await task.prompt(ListrEnquirerPromptAdapter).run({
              type: 'confirm',
              message: 'b',
            });
          },
        },
        {
          title: 'child2',
          task: async(ctx, task) => {
            await task.prompt(ListrEnquirerPromptAdapter).run({
              type: 'confirm',
              message: 'c',
            });
          },
        }
      ], { concurrent: false });
    }
  },
], { concurrent: false });

await task.run()
```

### Problem

When a parent task had a prompt, child tasks are unable to create their own prompts, even though the parent prompt did complete. I'm pretty sure that the `isPrompt()` function is incorrect:

https://github.com/listr2/listr2/blob/26c2cbdca6b6dabbaf3632557baf0ca549c3e230/packages/listr2/src/lib/task.ts#L233-L235

When the state is `PROMPT_COMPLETED`, this should return false. Here's my reasoning:

When the prompt completes,  it resets `activePrompt` back to `null`:

https://github.com/listr2/listr2/blob/26c2cbdca6b6dabbaf3632557baf0ca549c3e230/packages/listr2/src/renderer/default/renderer.ts#L301-L307

But since `isPrompt()` of the current task still returns `true`, even though the prompt already completed, it will immedietly set `activePrompt` back to the task ID on the next render iteration, before executing the child tasks:

https://github.com/listr2/listr2/blob/26c2cbdca6b6dabbaf3632557baf0ca549c3e230/packages/listr2/src/renderer/default/renderer.ts#L309

### Environment

I was certain that this was working at some point, but I bisected back to 8.0.0 and experienced the issue on every commit.

