### Support Request

I am trying to send all listr content to stderr, so that my CLI command output is pipeable to other commands (For example, to output some JSON at the end, which can be piped to `jq`). I would like to keep the normal output from DefaultRenderer output to the terminal.

I can see in the DefaultRenderer class, it's creating a logUpdate instance from `this.logger.process.stdout`.

However, trying to change seemingly relevant options doesn't seem to shift listr to using stderr instead of stdout. I have tried a few approaches, but I cannot figure out quite why it's not working.

I am testing a basic listr by calling `node build/index.js > out.log` - which will stream stdout to the file, but display stderr in the terminal, so for my ideal use case, the listr output should stay in the terminal, not be written to the file. In all cases, it keeps streaming the listr display output to the file.

#### I have tried:

Providing a custom logger & process output as `rendererOptions`:

```typescript
new Listr([], { 
  rendererOptions: { 
    logger: new ListrLogger({ processOutput: new ProcessOutput(process.stderr, process.stderr) }) 
  } 
})
```

Custom renderer class:

```typescript
class Renderer extends DefaultRenderer {
  constructor(tasks: any, options: any, events: any) {
    const processOutput = new ProcessOutput(process.stderr, process.stderr);
    const logger = new ListrLogger({ processOutput });

    super(tasks, {...(options || {}), logger}, events);
  }
}
```

I can't see any relevant issues/tickets in listr2 for this - there is one in the original listr1 repository, where someone asks for this functionality, but that has gotten no replies since 2020 as the project has moved here!

Am i doing something wrong here / any pointers would be appreciated!

