### Replication of the Problem

```js
import { Listr } from "listr2";

new Listr(
  [
    {
      title: "foo",
      task: (ctx, task) => {
        task.output = "bar";
      },
    },
  ],
  { disableColor: true },
).run();
```

### Problem

Even if `disableColor` option of `listr` is enabled, it is ignored and the output is colored.
The reason is that `createColors({ useColor: !process.env["LISTR_DISABLE_COLOR"]})` is called before evaluating `disableColor`.

